{"title":"2021 AMC 10B Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1_(Observations_and_Patterns:_Considers_Only_5_Squares)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1 (Observations and Patterns: Considers Only 5 Squares)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2_(Observations_and_Patterns:_Considers_Only_7_Squares)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2 (Observations and Patterns: Considers Only 7 Squares)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_3_(Brute_Force:_Draws_All_225_Squares_Out)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3 (Brute Force: Draws All 225 Squares Out)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_Pattern_Finding)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Pattern Finding)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Mr. Zhou places all the integers from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/1/5219cede5456639177ac2c4878419988f1867278.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$225$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> into a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/9/f1965fae079a9ba2c0726c307070c2355dfcb213.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$15$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> grid. He places <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> in the middle square (eighth row and eighth column) and places other numbers one by one clockwise, as shown in part in the diagram below. What is the sum of the greatest number and the least number that appear in the second row from the top?\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/d/2/2d2408a8772066f5c86886246eef174525a5b6a1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by samrocksnature */ add(grid(7,7)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (0.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (1.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (2.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (3.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (4.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (5.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (6.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (1.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (0.5,1.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (0.5,2.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (0.5,3.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (0.5,4.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (0.5,5.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (0.5,6.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (6.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (6.5,1.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (6.5,2.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (6.5,3.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (6.5,4.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (6.5,5.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (0.5,6.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (1.5,6.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (2.5,6.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (3.5,6.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (4.5,6.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (5.5,6.5)); label(&quot;$\\dots$&quot;, (6.5,6.5)); label(&quot;$17$&quot;, (1.5,1.5)); label(&quot;$18$&quot;, (1.5,2.5)); label(&quot;$19$&quot;, (1.5,3.5)); label(&quot;$20$&quot;, (1.5,4.5)); label(&quot;$21$&quot;, (1.5,5.5)); label(&quot;$16$&quot;, (2.5,1.5)); label(&quot;$5$&quot;, (2.5,2.5)); label(&quot;$6$&quot;, (2.5,3.5)); label(&quot;$7$&quot;, (2.5,4.5)); label(&quot;$22$&quot;, (2.5,5.5)); label(&quot;$15$&quot;, (3.5,1.5)); label(&quot;$4$&quot;, (3.5,2.5)); label(&quot;$1$&quot;, (3.5,3.5)); label(&quot;$8$&quot;, (3.5,4.5)); label(&quot;$23$&quot;, (3.5,5.5)); label(&quot;$14$&quot;, (4.5,1.5)); label(&quot;$3$&quot;, (4.5,2.5)); label(&quot;$2$&quot;, (4.5,3.5)); label(&quot;$9$&quot;, (4.5,4.5)); label(&quot;$24$&quot;, (4.5,5.5)); label(&quot;$13$&quot;, (5.5,1.5)); label(&quot;$12$&quot;, (5.5,2.5)); label(&quot;$11$&quot;, (5.5,3.5)); label(&quot;$10$&quot;, (5.5,4.5)); label(&quot;$25$&quot;, (5.5,5.5)); [/asy]\" width=\"252\" height=\"252\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/a/03a95e58766401af8575bf01e0ab65cb82a77f3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)} ~367 \\qquad\\textbf{(B)} ~368 \\qquad\\textbf{(C)} ~369 \\qquad\\textbf{(D)} ~379 \\qquad\\textbf{(E)} ~380$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"439\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_1_.28Observations_and_Patterns:_Considers_Only_5_Squares.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1_(Observations_and_Patterns:_Considers_Only_5_Squares)\">Solution 1 (Observations and Patterns: Considers Only 5 Squares)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1 (Observations and Patterns: Considers Only 5 Squares)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram below, the red arrows indicate the progression of numbers. In the second row from the top, the greatest number and the least number are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/a/a0a1dbdebe8f3df1befc34f5862f69364b3c11b6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$E,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> respectively. Note that the numbers in the yellow cells are consecutive odd perfect squares, as we can prove by induction.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/c/5ac813fa4bb2f809f3bc13e834eb8dbda9982c18.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy]  /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(11.5cm);  for (real i=7.5; i&lt;=14.5; ++i)  { \tfill((i+0.5,i+0.5)--(i-0.5,i+0.5)--(i-0.5,i-0.5)--(i+0.5,i-0.5)--cycle,yellow); }  fill((2,14)--(1,14)--(1,13)--(2,13)--cycle,green); fill((1,14)--(0,14)--(0,13)--(1,13)--cycle,green);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(14.5,14.5)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(13.5,13.5)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(0.5,14.5)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,(1.5,13.5)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(0.5,13.5));  add(grid(15,15,linewidth(1.25)));  draw((1.5,13.5)--(14.5,13.5)--(14.5,0.5)--(0.5,0.5)--(0.5,14.5)--(14.5,14.5),red+linewidth(1.125),EndArrow); [/asy]\" width=\"545\" height=\"545\" />\nBy observations, we proceed as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/a/68a31ee8a74a5a954e0a9311b76db33aa37ca1c1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{alignat*}{6} A=15^2=225, \\ B=13^2=169  \\quad &amp;\\implies \\quad &amp;C &amp;= \\hspace{1mm}&amp;&amp;A-14\\hspace{1mm} &amp;= 211&amp; \\\\  \\quad &amp;\\implies \\quad &amp;D &amp;= &amp;&amp;C-1  &amp;= 210&amp; \\\\  \\quad &amp;\\implies \\quad &amp;E &amp;= &amp;&amp;B-12 &amp;= 157&amp;.  \\end{alignat*}\" width=\"470\" height=\"65\" />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/9/4/c94c5be45030b251db895c055baaf47033346c8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D+E=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} ~367}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"153\" height=\"28\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_2_.28Observations_and_Patterns:_Considers_Only_7_Squares.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2_(Observations_and_Patterns:_Considers_Only_7_Squares)\">Solution 2 (Observations and Patterns: Considers Only 7 Squares)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2 (Observations and Patterns: Considers Only 7 Squares)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the diagram below, the red arrows indicate the progression of numbers. In the second row from the top, the greatest number and the least number are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/5/195d683ae02c57abf49ebe0889c6f2ea7bcc513e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$G,$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"18\" height=\"16\" /> respectively.\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/3/73369ee63a71ed2b97db5a0051a801bff54efde0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(11.5cm);  fill((2,14)--(1,14)--(1,13)--(2,13)--cycle,green); fill((1,14)--(0,14)--(0,13)--(1,13)--cycle,green);  label(&quot;$A$&quot;,(14.5,14.5)); label(&quot;$B$&quot;,(0.5,14.5)); label(&quot;$C$&quot;,(0.5,13.5)); label(&quot;$D$&quot;,(0.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$E$&quot;,(14.5,0.5)); label(&quot;$F$&quot;,(14.5,13.5)); label(&quot;$G$&quot;,(1.5,13.5));  add(grid(15,15,linewidth(1.25)));  draw((1.5,13.5)--(14.5,13.5)--(14.5,0.5)--(0.5,0.5)--(0.5,14.5)--(14.5,14.5),red+linewidth(1.125),EndArrow); [/asy]\" width=\"545\" height=\"545\" />\nBy observations, we proceed as follows:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/0/0/a00f017985712124ad24d9a1f764084afdc4a61d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\begin{alignat*}{6} A=15^2=225  \\quad &amp;\\implies \\quad &amp;B &amp;= \\hspace{1mm}&amp;&amp;A-14\\hspace{1mm} &amp;= 211&amp; \\\\  \\quad &amp;\\implies \\quad &amp;C &amp;= &amp;&amp;B-1  &amp;= 210&amp; \\\\  \\quad &amp;\\implies \\quad &amp;D &amp;= &amp;&amp;C-13 &amp;= 197&amp; \\\\ \\quad &amp;\\implies \\quad &amp;E &amp;= &amp;&amp;D-14 &amp;= 183&amp; \\\\ \\quad &amp;\\implies \\quad &amp;F &amp;= &amp;&amp;E-13 &amp;= 170&amp; \\\\ \\quad &amp;\\implies \\quad &amp;G &amp;= &amp;&amp;F-13 &amp;= 157&amp;.  \\end{alignat*}\" width=\"340\" height=\"140\" />\nTherefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/3/d/03d336916c361a64af7fea8cb609f565d10be81a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C+G=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} ~367}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"155\" height=\"30\" />\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM ~Dynosol\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Solution_3_.28Brute_Force:_Draws_All_225_Squares_Out.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3_(Brute_Force:_Draws_All_225_Squares_Out)\">Solution 3 (Brute Force: Draws All 225 Squares Out)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3 (Brute Force: Draws All 225 Squares Out)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From the full diagram below, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/d/91d5c9b191f3be68dc22de7c232ed7525b55b488.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$210+157=\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)} ~367}.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"178\" height=\"28\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/6/0f635e1a8e3482a6105ddacbce422ea12708b96c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"[asy] /* Made by MRENTHUSIASM */ size(11.5cm);  fill((2,14)--(1,14)--(1,13)--(2,13)--cycle,green); fill((1,14)--(0,14)--(0,13)--(1,13)--cycle,green);  add(grid(15,15,linewidth(1.25)));  int adj = 1; int curDown = 2; int curLeft = 4; int curUp = 6; int curRight = 8;  label(&quot;$1$&quot;,(7.5,7.5));  for (int len = 3; len&lt;=15; len+=2) { \tfor (int i=1; i&lt;=len-1; ++i)     \t\t{ \t\t\tlabel(&quot;$&quot;+string(curDown)+&quot;$&quot;,(7.5+adj,7.5+adj-i));     \t\tlabel(&quot;$&quot;+string(curLeft)+&quot;$&quot;,(7.5+adj-i,7.5-adj));      \t\tlabel(&quot;$&quot;+string(curUp)+&quot;$&quot;,(7.5-adj,7.5-adj+i));     \t\tlabel(&quot;$&quot;+string(curRight)+&quot;$&quot;,(7.5-adj+i,7.5+adj));     \t\t++curDown;     \t\t++curLeft;     \t\t++curUp;     \t\t++curRight; \t\t} \t++adj;     curDown = len^2 + 1;     curLeft = len^2 + len + 2;     curUp = len^2 + 2*len + 3;     curRight = len^2 + 3*len + 4; } [/asy]\" width=\"545\" height=\"545\" />\n<b>This solution is extremely time-consuming and error-prone. Please do not try it in a real competition unless you have no other options.</b>\n</p><p>~MRENTHUSIASM ~Taco12\n</p>\n<h2><span id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_.28Using_Pattern_Finding.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_OmegaLearn_(Using_Pattern_Finding)\">Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Pattern Finding)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by OmegaLearn (Using Pattern Finding)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/bb4HB7pwO3Q\">https://youtu.be/bb4HB7pwO3Q</a>\n</p><p>~ pi_is_3.14\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_TheBeautyofMath\">Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by TheBeautyofMath\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/GYpAm8v1h-U?t=412\">https://youtu.be/GYpAm8v1h-U?t=412</a>\n</p><p>~IceMatrix\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Interstigation\">Video Solution by Interstigation</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2021_AMC_10B_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Interstigation\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/DvpN56Ob6Zw?t=667\">https://youtu.be/DvpN56Ob6Zw?t=667</a>\n</p><p>~Interstigation\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a hr